    "answer": "```json\n{\n  \"findings\": \"The test suite is a single monolithic project (`tests/VisualRelay.Tests/VisualRelay.Tests.csproj`, net10.0) containing ~322 xUnit test files covering all source and tool projects. xUnit is already configured for parallel collection execution (`xunit.runner.json` has `parallelizeTestCollections: true`), and the codebase has mature infrastructure for safe parallelization:\\n\\n- **Headless collection** (`[CollectionDefinition(\\\"Headless\\\")]` in `HeadlessCollectionDefinition.cs`): Serializes ~47 test classes that use `[AvaloniaFact]`/`[AvaloniaTheory]` because they share one process-global Avalonia dispatcher. A convention guard test (`SplitGuardVerificationTests.Headless.cs`) enforces that every class with Avalonia test attributes carries this attribute.\\n- **Watchdog collection** (`[Collection(\\\"Watchdog\\\")]` on `SwivalSubagentRunnerWatchdogTests`): Serializes CPU-burning subprocess tests, though notably there is NO `CollectionDefinition` for it \u2014 xUnit v3 still serializes within the collection but the definition is absent.\\n- **Environment isolation**: Convention guard (`SplitGuardVerificationTests.Conventions.cs`) bans `Environment.SetEnvironmentVariable` calls in tests (with documented exemptions). `TestModuleInitializer` sets `XDG_CONFIG_HOME` to a unique per-process temp dir. Most tests use injected `IEnvironmentAccessor` rather than process-global env state.\\n- **Isolated test repositories**: `TestRepository.Create()` provides fresh per-test temp repos.\\n\\n**The bottleneck** is `-m:1` (MaxCpuCount=1) passed to `dotnet test` in three locations, which forces fully sequential execution despite xUnit's parallelization settings:\\n\\n1. `tools/VisualRelay.Cli/TestRunner.cs:29` \u2014 `\\\"test\\\", paths.TestsProject, \\\"-m:1\\\", ...` (the `visual-relay test` command)\\n2. `tools/VisualRelay.Cli/Commands/CheckCommand.cs:49` \u2014 `\\\"test\\\", paths.TestsProject, \\\"-m:1\\\", ...` (the `visual-relay check` command's test step)\\n3. `tools/dotnet-test-files.sh:16,18` \u2014 `dotnet test \\\"$proj\\\" -m:1 ...` (the targeted test file runner invoked by the harness)\\n\\nBuild steps also use `-m:1` (CheckCommand.cs:32 build, CheckCommand.cs:66 screenshots build, BuildCommand.cs:17 build, InstallHooksCommand.cs:38) but those are separate from test execution.\\n\\nAdditional notes:\\n- `TestRunner.cs` and `CheckCommand.cs` both wrap `dotnet test` with `TimeoutWatchdog` (default 60s for `test`, 300s for `check`).\\n- The `TestCommand`/`TestFileCommand` config system is tested by `TargetedTestCommandTests.cs`.\\n- The CI workflow (`release.yml`) only builds/publishes artifacts and does NOT run the test suite.\\n- The repo's `Directory.Build.targets` contains a `GuardSourceEnumeration` MSBuild task to detect stale virtio-fs readdir caches.\\n\\n**Conclusion**: The Headless and Watchdog collections already provide the serialization safety needed for option 3 from the ideate stage (remove `-m:1` and annotate serial-only tests). The one-time audit for serial-only tests has already largely been done \u2014 the existing collection architecture and convention guards mean removing `-m:1` is low-risk. An explicit `[CollectionDefinition(\\\"Watchdog\\\")]` should be added for completeness.\",\n  \"constraints\": [\n    \"All tests using [AvaloniaFact] or [AvaloniaTheory] MUST remain in [Collection(\\\"Headless\\\")] \u2014 enforced by an existing reflection-based convention guard (SplitGuardVerificationTests.Headless.cs).\",\n    \"Watchdog tests that launch real CPU-burning subprocesses (SwivalSubagentRunnerWatchdogTests and companions) MUST remain serialized \u2014 they currently use [Collection(\\\"Watchdog\\\")] but lack a CollectionDefinition, which should be added.\",\n    \"Environment.SetEnvironmentVariable is banned in test files except for documented exemptions (TestModuleInitializer.cs, TestDoubles.cs, RepoSetup.cs, BackendLifecycleStatusTests.cs, KeyEnvFileHermeticityTests.cs, HeadlessTestApp.cs, and the conventions file itself) \u2014 enforced by convention guard.\",\n    \"The `-m:1` flag must be removed or adjusted in THREE places for tests: TestRunner.cs line 29, CheckCommand.cs line 49, and tools/dotnet-test-files.sh lines 16/18. Build-time `-m:1` usages (CheckCommand.cs:32/66, BuildCommand.cs:17, InstallHooksCommand.cs:38) are a separate concern and should NOT be changed.\",\n    \"Test timeout watchdog defaults (60s test, 300s check) are independent of -m and do not need adjustment, but their interaction with parallelism (more tests running simultaneously consuming wall-clock timeout budget) may need consideration.\",\n    \"The TestModuleInitializer sets XDG_CONFIG_HOME to a single per-process temp dir \u2014 this is safe because production code uses injected IEnvironmentAccessor, but it is a shared mutable process-level env var that could theoretically race if any test reads it directly.\",\n    \"dotnet-test-files.sh is the harness's targeted test runner and must be kept in sync with the other two files for consistent behavior.\",\n    \"ControlServerTests has a static readonly HttpClient \u2014 this is immutable/shared but safe; any test that mutates HttpClient state would be a problem.\",\n    \"The solution file (VisualRelay.slnx) declares only one test project under /tests/ \u2014 splitting into multiple projects (option 2) would require modifying the solution and project references.\"\n  ]\n}\n```",
